# Requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client):
# click "Send Request" above each request.
# `make run` and `docker compose up` both use GANTRY_TOKEN from .env.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:7070
@token = {{$dotenv GANTRY_TOKEN}}

### Health (public, no token)
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Version
GET {{host}}/api/v1/version
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List stacks
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stack details
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unknown stack → 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/does-not-exist
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid name → 400
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/Bad.Name
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks

# --- Actions ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Actions run as operations: the response (202) contains the operation's id.
# Follow it with "Operation" below, or live in a terminal:
#   curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer dev" http://127.0.0.1:7070/api/v1/operations/<id>/events

### Start whoami (docker compose up -d)
# @name start
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami/actions/start
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Operation with output (of the last "Start whoami")
GET {{host}}/api/v1/operations/{{start.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restart whoami
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami/actions/restart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update whoami (pull new images, recreate changed containers)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami/actions/update
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stop whoami (containers are kept)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami/actions/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Down whoami (removes containers and networks, never volumes)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami/actions/down
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel the last "Start whoami" → 409 if it has already finished
POST {{host}}/api/v1/operations/{{start.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recent operations of whoami
GET {{host}}/api/v1/operations?stack=whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unknown action → 400
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/whoami/actions/explode
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a stack "scratch"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "scratch", "compose": "services:\n  app:\n    image: traefik/whoami:v1.12\n", "env": {"GREETING": "hello"}}

### Details of scratch, with the Compose file's version
# @name scratch
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace scratch's Compose file (409 version_conflict if it changed meanwhile)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch/compose
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "{{scratch.response.body.composeFile.version}}", "content": "services:\n  app:\n    image: traefik/whoami:v1.12\n    restart: unless-stopped\n"}

### Invalid Compose file → 400 invalid_compose, file unchanged
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch/compose
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "{{scratch.response.body.composeFile.version}}", "content": "services:\n  app:\n    ports: 80\n"}

### .env variable names of scratch (no values)
# @name env
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch/env
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Set and delete .env variables
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch/env
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "{{env.response.body.version}}", "set": {"DB_PASSWORD": "it's a $ecret"}, "delete": ["GREETING"]}

### Show one .env value (logged by the agent, without the value)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch/env/reveal
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "DB_PASSWORD"}

### Delete scratch permanently (directory included; volumes only with volumes=true)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/stacks/scratch?confirm=scratch
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
